From: Carlos Cabrera H. <6750732+ccabrerah@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH 26] ggml-sycl: oneDNN matmuls in deterministic mode (GGML_SYCL_DNNL_DETERMINISTIC)

GGML_SYCL_DNNL_DETERMINISTIC=1 sets oneDNN's deterministic attribute on the DnnlGemmWrapper matmul (the bf16/f16
GEMM path). oneDNN may split a long reduction across work-groups and add the partial sums atomically; the same matmul
on the same inputs then differs in the last bits between runs (measured on this model: the hyper-connection mixer's
bf16 [10240 x 320] x f32 [10240 x 1024] at the start of every layer, different bits on a rerun in one process), and
greedy text diverges at near-ties. With the attribute every run of a graph gives the same bits.

--- a/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/gemm.hpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/gemm.hpp
@@ -56,6 +56,11 @@
         const auto c_md    = dnnl::memory::desc(c_dims, ct, c_strides);
         dnnl::primitive_attr primitive_attr;
         primitive_attr.set_scratchpad_mode(dnnl::scratchpad_mode::user);
+        // GGML_SYCL_DNNL_DETERMINISTIC=1: oneDNN may split a long reduction (K) across work-groups and add the partial
+        // sums atomically, so the same matmul on the same inputs differs in the last bits from run to run. Its
+        // deterministic attribute forbids that; with it every run of a graph gives the same bits.
+        static const bool deterministic = [] { const char * e = getenv("GGML_SYCL_DNNL_DETERMINISTIC"); return e && atoi(e) != 0; }();
+        if (deterministic) primitive_attr.set_deterministic(true);
 
 #ifdef GGML_SYCL_F16
         primitive_attr.set_fpmath_mode(dnnl::fpmath_mode::f16);
